<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Strict//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-strict.dtd">
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
    <head>
        <title>Centered text stays centered in a wider definite box</title>
        <!-- Engine bug pinned: a "fits by definition" guard switched
             wider-than-content text nodes to MaxContent layout, but
             Definite(w) is ALSO the alignment container width - centered
             captions (the ribbon's "Clipboard"/"Font" group labels)
             rendered left-anchored. -->
        <style type="text/css">
            * { margin: 0; padding: 0; }
            body { width: 800px; background: #ffffff; font-family: sans-serif; }
            .caption { width: 600px; text-align: center; font-size: 28px;
                       color: #444444; background: #f1f1f1; padding: 8px 0; margin: 6px 0; }
            .caption2 { width: 600px; text-align: right; font-size: 28px;
                        color: #444444; background: #e4e4e4; padding: 8px 0; }
        </style>
    </head>
    <body>
        <div class="caption">Clipboard</div>
        <div class="caption2">Font</div>
    </body>
</html>
